  "riskDisclosure": {
    "title": "Contract Trading Risk Disclosure",
    "cancel": "Cancel",
    "confirm": "Confirm and Enable Contract Trading",
    "content": {
      "paragraph1": "1. When trading in the contract market, if market movements are unfavorable and cause losses, leading to insufficient position margin, your positions will be subject to forced liquidation according to system rules. Liquidation details will be disclosed.",
      "paragraph2": "2. Please carefully read and follow our trading rules. Understand the contract mechanisms and operating principles, be aware of various market risks, and manage your funds reasonably when trading.",
      "paragraph3": "3. In extreme market conditions, you may find it difficult or impossible to close your open positions. For example, if your profit ranks first in effective leverage PnL across the contract market, and the insurance fund is insufficient to cover the liquidation losses of the losing side.",
      "paragraph4": "4. Due to changes in local laws, regulations, policies, contract exchange trading rules, or implementation of emergency measures, we will announce in advance if your open positions cannot be maintained. However, the platform will still honor position margins and profits!",
      "paragraph5": "5. Due to factors beyond our control, such as earthquakes, floods, fires, or other force majeure events, or computer system and communication system failures, your orders may not be executed or may be partially executed, potentially resulting in losses.",
      "paragraph6": "6. 'Hedging' trades face the same price fluctuation risks as speculative trades. Please understand the relevant mechanisms in advance.",
      "paragraph7": "7. If you allow others to operate your account, it may affect your contract margin safety. Please ensure your personal account security."
    }
  },
